  "title": "Erdős Problem #302",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(N)$ be the size of the largest $A\\subseteq \\{1,\\ldots,N\\}$ such that there are no solutions to $ \\frac{1}{a}= \\frac{1}{b}+\\frac{1}{c} $ with distinct $a,b,c\\in A$?\nEstimate $f(N)$. In particular, is $f(N)=(\\tfrac{1}{2}+o(1))N$?",
